    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for gdb.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The GNU Debugger (GDB) allows debugging programs written in C, C++, Java, and\nother languages by executing them in a controlled fashion and then printing\ntheir data.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* gdb: STABS debug format parser out-of-bounds write via crafted ELF binary (CVE-2026-13732)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS\nscore, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE\npage(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
